# Clean code

Write code a teammate can read once. Prefer small pure functions and explicit contracts over nested guards.

- Transform data. Do not repeat the same absence check through every layer.
- Narrow `null` / `undefined` at the boundary. After that, work with values.
- Optional arguments that mean “maybe also do this other thing” are a smell. Take what the function needs.
- Name the condition instead of chaining `!== undefined` and `!== null`.
- Prefer `map` / `filter` / a lookup helper over index arithmetic and leftover fallbacks.
- Do not add defensive checks to silence TypeScript. Fix the type or the algorithm.
- Functional means values in, values out — not a library, not `pipe` everywhere, not hidden control flow.
